          Nutrition facts and caloric databases almost universally reference raw, uncooked food weights unless stated otherwise. Cooking fundamentally alters weight through moisture loss (meats shrink 20% to 30%, making them more calorie-dense) or water absorption (rice and pasta expand 2 to 3 times, diluting calorie density). If measuring cooked meals or batch meal prep, convert values using the <a href="https://rawtocookedcalculator.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-ink font-medium underline underline-offset-2 hover:opacity-80 transition-opacity">Raw to Cooked Calculator</a> to ensure your daily calorie tracking remains exact.
